Third-party components
----------------------

Photonation depends on third-party crates that keep their own licences. All of
them are compatible with GPL-3.0-or-later; `cargo deny check licenses`
(configured in deny.toml) enforces the allowed set in CI. Notable ones:

rawler (https://github.com/dnglab/dnglab), LGPL-2.1
  Camera raw decoding, used by crates/raw. LGPL-2.1 section 3 permits applying
  the GPL (version 2 or later) instead, so it combines with this GPL-3.0 work.

Inter (https://github.com/rsms/inter), SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Copyright 2020 The Inter Project Authors. The interface font, embedded in the
  desktop binary; the licence is in assets/fonts/OFL-Inter.txt.

Sora (https://github.com/sora-xor/sora-font), SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Copyright 2019 The Sora Project Authors. The display font for the wordmark,
  embedded in the desktop binary; the licence is in assets/fonts/OFL-Sora.txt.

egui default fonts (epaint_default_fonts): Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0 and
SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Embedded in the desktop binary as fallback fonts. Both licences explicitly
  allow bundling the fonts with any software; the fonts remain under their own
  licences.

jpeg-encoder: (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND IJG
  Includes code derived from the Independent JPEG Group's software. This
  software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

tract (https://github.com/sonos/tract), MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Pure-Rust ONNX runtime, used by crates/retouch (feature "onnx") to run
  neural inpainting models. Copyright the tract contributors / Sonos. Its
  dependency tree is permissive: mostly MIT OR Apache-2.0, plus MIT-only
  (bytes, nom, libm, metrics, derive-new, ...), Apache-2.0-only (prost,
  prost-derive), Zlib (foldhash) and Unicode-3.0 (unicode-ident). None of
  these crates ships an Apache NOTICE file that would have to be passed on.

Obligations when distributing binaries
--------------------------------------

MIT, BSD, Unicode-3.0 and the font licences require their copyright and
permission notices to accompany every copy, and Apache-2.0 (section 4)
requires a copy of the licence text. Source distributions satisfy this
through the crates' own licence files. Binary distributions (app bundles,
installers) must include the licence texts of every compiled-in crate, for
example as a generated THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES file. We modify none of these
crates; if that changes, Apache-2.0 section 4(b) requires the modified files
to say so.

Inpainting models (not distributed)
-----------------------------------

Photonation does not ship neural network weights. The "Generative AI"
removal method loads a model file the user installs (see docs/RETOUCH.md):

LaMa (https://github.com/advimman/lama), Apache-2.0
  Resolution-robust Large Mask Inpainting with Fourier Convolutions,
  Suvorov et al. 2021. ONNX exports are third-party conversions.

MI-GAN (https://github.com/Picsart-AI-Research/MI-GAN), MIT
  Mobile Inpainting GAN, Sargsyan et al. 2023, Picsart AI Research.

Anyone who bundles one of these models with Photonation must include that
model's licence (and, for LaMa, any NOTICE file of the upstream project).
